<p id="p2">In a post by <a href="https://x.com/gregjoz/status/2112212372182249831" rel="noopener noreferrer">Greg Joswiak on X</a>, Apple has said it will hold an ‘Pro and Tell’ in Los Angeles, California on Wednesday, October 28 at 10:00 am Pacific.</p>
<p id="p3">Judging from the ‘Pro’ in the tagline, I wouldn’t be surprised if we see <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/12/new-macs-and-ipad-mini-in-los-angeles/" rel="noopener noreferrer">the much rumored</a> touch-screen MacBook Pro at the event. Other rumors point to a possible refresh of the iMac and the iPad mini.</p>
<p id="p4">Our very own Federico will be there in person to cover the event, and of course we’ll have written coverage here on MacStories and later on AppStories.</p>
